# Implementation Plan: Hangfire + PostgreSQL Persistence

Integrate **Hangfire** with **PostgreSQL Database Persistence** in ASP.NET Core to ensure 100% background job crash survival, automatic retries, and real-time job monitoring via `/hangfire` dashboard.

---

## Why Hangfire vs Kafka?

```mermaid
graph TD
    subgraph HealSync Web Architecture
        A[ASP.NET Core Web API] -->|Enqueues Job| B[Hangfire Job Processor]
        B -->|Persists Job State| C[(PostgreSQL Database)]
        B -->|Executes Background| D[Email & WebPush Service]
    end
```

| Criteria | Hangfire (Chosen Solution) | Apache Kafka |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Infrastructure Overhead** | **Zero extra servers** (Uses existing PostgreSQL DB) | Requires multi-broker Kafka/Zookeeper cluster servers |
| **Integration Complexity** | Native .NET C# extension | Complex Java/Scala binary broker orchestration |
| **Crash Survival** | **100% DB Persisted** in PostgreSQL | 100% Persisted in Kafka Commit Log |
| **Dashboard UI** | Included native web UI (`/hangfire`) | Requires 3rd-party UI (Confluent / AKHQ) |
| **Best Fit** | Monolithic & Modular .NET Web APIs (HealSync) | Distributed microservice networks (Uber, Netflix) |

